    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d518">

                <pb facs="0432" n="420" xml:id="pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.20/565: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-20T11:00:00-00:44">May 20, 1942—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>156. Department’s 113, May 16, 9 p.m. I have discussed with President Barclay the
                    question of Germans leaving Liberia and informed him of the statement of the War
                    Department in regard to the early arrival of adequate forces which will enable
                    him to submit the agreement to the legislature.</p>
                <p>President Barclay agrees with the suggestion concerning the Germans and states
                    that the German Consul General has already been informally notified that if
                    circumstances should change here the Germans would be invited to leave the
                    country. President Barclay now states that he will immediately invite the
                    Germans to leave Liberia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
